{#
  What the judge decides about the application, which starts the order's wording, on one row as the rest of
  the make order page asks its questions. Using the applicant's wording puts it in the order preview as the
  judge's own clauses, which the reset button restores. Listing it for a hearing on notice asks when, as
  the adjournment tab does, and leaves the application open. Inline radios can't reveal a question, so what
  follows a decision is on its own rows, shown while it is chosen (initApplicationDecision in make-order.ts).
#}
{% import "make-order/_compact.njk" as compact with context %}
{% import "make-order/_listing.njk" as listing with context %}

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l govuk-!-margin-top-6">Decision</h2>

{{ compact.radios("application-decision", {
  legend: "What do you decide?",
  legendHidden: true,
  hint: "For something else, write the order in the order preview. In any case, you may amend the wording in the order preview.",
  classes: "govuk-radios--small govuk-radios--inline",
  items: [
    { value: "grant", text: "Use the applicant’s wording" },
    { value: "dismiss", text: "Dismiss" },
    { value: "strike-out", text: "Strike out" },
    { value: "list", text: "List for a hearing on notice" },
    { value: "other", text: "Something else" }
  ]
}) }}

{% if application.whatOrderWanted %}
  <div data-decision-shows="grant" {%- if not draftChecked("application-decision", "grant") %} hidden{% endif %}>
    <button type="button" class="govuk-button govuk-button--secondary" data-restore-requested-wording>
      Reset to applicant’s wording
    </button>
  </div>
{% endif %}

<div data-decision-shows="list" data-application-listing {%- if not draftChecked("application-decision", "list") %} hidden{% endif %}>
  {{ listing.listing("list", "When the hearing is", [
    "Next available possession list after",
    "Next available date (non-possession list) after",
    "Specific date"
  ]) }}
</div>
